WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.332 --> 00:00:07.140
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.350
Hi, everyone.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.740
My name is Daniella
Smalls-Perkins.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.950
And my name is Dorris Scott.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.760
And we are the co-founders
of Mi-R community.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.230
Today, during this
lighting talk,

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.960
we're going to reflect a
little bit on Mi-R community

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.410
this past year and also invite
you to join some of the efforts

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.430
that we plan to carry
out in the next year.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.570
I'll first start with the hope
for Mi-R. So the hope for Mi-R

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.870
is to promote the visibility
and leadership of R users

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:39.350
from marginalized races,
genders, the LGBTQ community,

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.780
and the disabled community
through community

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.870
led efforts that support
professional development.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.430
Right now, we have slightly
under 200 members and allies

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.340
within our community slack
from different countries,

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.460
backgrounds, experiences,
and all flavors

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:00.285
of data people, data scientists,
data analysts, et cetera.

00:01:00.285 --> 00:01:01.910
All of these folks
are willing to share

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.360
their unique perspectives
and their love of R.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.230
Some of the highlights
from this past year really,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.780
first, of course, is
just getting the group

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.990
off the ground and starting
to see people roll in.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:20.330
We started right as the
pandemic hit the entire world

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:26.420
and tried to garner support
and momentum just as the US

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.970
was going through a
racial reckoning-- excuse

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.850
me, a reckoning
for racial justice.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:35.720
So to see the
outpouring of support,

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.610
Allison Horst designed
logo and graphics for us

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.400
to see other members join
and support each other

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.290
and lead new initiatives.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.390
That's just been truly special.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.330
Another huge highlight
of this past year

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.450
were the webinars
held by our community members.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.840
Darren Ramsland led
a webinar focused

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.380
on some of the new features
in the recently updated dplyr

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:03.200
and then some of his
favorite functions

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.330
associated with that library.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:11.420
Also, Shel Kariuki, provided
a webinar focused on ggplot2

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.120
and shared some of
her tips and tricks

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.430
when doing data visualization.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.930
We also had an RStudio
instructor certification panel

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:24.515
led by Greg Wilson, Shel
Kariuki, Yanina Bellini

00:02:24.515 --> 00:02:27.740
Saibene, in which they
talked about the process

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:32.390
to become an RStudio
certified instructor.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.930
And we've also been having
some study sessions every month

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.960
for those that are
preparing to take the exam

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.380
to become an RStudio
certified instructor.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.160
So those are some of
the top highlights.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.740
I'll now pass it
to Dorris to share

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:51.830
a couple more reflections.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:56.390
I have a lot of reflections
on how our first year went

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.010
as an organization.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:03.080
But for the sake of time, I will
just share only one reflection.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.480
We originally created
Mi-R because we

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:08.060
wanted to create a space
in which people who did not

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.190
see themselves in the
data science community

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.810
could come together.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:15.470
We hope that Mi-R would
extend past our ability

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:19.220
to adequately support all of the
intersectional backgrounds that

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.600
are in the community.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.460
And indeed, it has.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.700
We are so grateful for
members of our community

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.910
who provide their unique
perspectives, insights,

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.740
knowledge, and skills.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:34.310
Thank you so much for all that
you bring to our community.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.910
In 2021, we are working
on several endeavors.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:40.160
We don't want to give
away our full lineup.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.720
So here's a preview
of what's to come.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.480
We are currently
working on endeavors

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.170
to ensure that Mi-R webinars
are accessible to Mi-R members

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.400
with disabilities along with
the wider community of R users

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.660
with disabilities.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.580
And we are working
on a Tidy Tuesday

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.370
event in which we will
focus on best practices

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:01.250
to make R visualizations
more accessible.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.490
In addition, we intend to have
more professional development

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:07.550
workshops such as resume
workshops and interview

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.280
preparedness, along
with a digital security

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:15.950
webinar for researchers sharing
their work with the public.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:20.350
So if you identify as an
underrepresented R user,

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:23.090
then we invite you to join
Mi-R community as a member.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.210
And if you'd like to
support the community

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:29.860
but don't necessarily identify
as an underrepresented R user,

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.230
then we would love to
have you join as an ally

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.790
in support of the members.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.570
You can find us on Twitter
and YouTube @mircommunity.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:44.150
And you can also visit us
at www.mircommuntiy.com.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.310
Thanks so much for
listening to our talk.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.250
DORRIS SCOTT: Thank you.

